	(text "U7: Tokmas ICM-42688-P (C54308212); TDK eval board as reference (D-09).\nFB2 with C44-C46 gives the IMU its own filtered rail, +3V3_IMU.\nR58 holds CS high: the IMU ignores the bus while the ESP32 is in reset (D-19).\nINT2/FSYNC is unused: R56 ties it to GND."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 172.466 222.758 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "136de2d0-b40e-4628-83cf-f11db0612aed")
	)
	(text "ESP32-WROOM-32E-N4  (GPIO map: SPEC.md section 3)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 22.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2fb85ebb-563a-4805-bc14-abaf74f2fb5b")
	)
	(text "strapping pins: IO0 (BOOT), IO2 (LIDAR_EN, 10k down), IO12 (ACT_IN2, 10k down),\nIO15 (LED data, CMOS input only), IO5 (rear UART TX, idles high).\nAnalog inputs are all on ADC1 (IO32-39). IO14 chirps the buzzer for a few ms at boot."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 158.75 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "6a460609-e7c2-4d85-b016-5c290e19e2e6")
	)
	(text "J17 VBUS (A9/B4) feeds only the 3.3 V LDO, through D5 on the power sheet (D-10).\nA4/B9 are VBUS_ALT, a net of their own: every plug joins all four VBUS contacts (D-19).\nR59 (0 ohm) is the one D+/D- crossing, so the pair stays on the top layer (D-19).\nCC1/CC2 5.1k to GND: the host sees a USB device. or should. U15: D-, CC2, VBUS; U17: D+, CC1."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 172.974 157.988 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a146fd6c-b418-4a84-8b4f-5ac274c949fe")
	)
	(text "CH340C ~DTR high, ~RTS low: Q6 on, EN low (reset).  ~DTR low, ~RTS high: Q7 on, IO0 low (boot).\nboth equal: both off. JP1 is closed by default; cut it once the firmware is stable,\nso the Pi opening the port can't reset the ESP32 mid-drive (D-11)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.526 277.114 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "cce1a22b-e99a-4508-8d7a-58f2567bc234")
	)
